/* ==================== Script 1245 id="amiyo-export2-s02-verified" ==================== */
/* Export round 2, step 2 checked (presets, sizes, fps, range, parts): all 14 presets, the 5 size chips, 6 frame rates, 6 range choices (incl. bad custom times) and the part split (10/20/30 min, start-at-part, range + parts) were run in the editor and gave the sizes, frame rates, ranges and file names shown in "Will make". Four faults fixed: (1) after a preset that switches the canvas (Reels, Story, Instagram...) the Custom size boxes still used the OLD canvas shape, so Custom size / Match project gave a wrong-shaped file; (2) empty custom width/height boxes silently exported 160x160; (3) a one-file export that used a part length got "-part1of1" in its name and part toasts; (4) "Start at part 9" with only 3 parts silently started at part 3 - it is now corrected in the box with a message, and the box is hidden when there is only one part. Not testable here: MP4/H.264 (the test browser has no H.264) and real frame counts (the test machine has 1 slow CPU, so the export fell back to the live recorder). */window.AMIYO_EXPORT2_STEP=2;

;
/* ==================== Script 1246 id="amiyo-export2-s03-verified" ==================== */
/* Export round 2, step 3 checked (WAV and Audio button): real WAV files were written for all 5 presets and 4 manual rate/bit/channel combinations and read back with ffprobe/ffmpeg: right sample rate, bit depth, channels, length (8.003 s, 600.0 s for a 10 minute edit), no decode errors; "loudest point -1 dB" gave exactly -1.0 dB; In -> Out (4.0 s), selected clip (6.0 s), muted video track, solo audio track, 2 s fades (-41 dB at both ends), speed 2, clip volume, track fader (-6 dB each), hard-left pan (right channel silent) and cancel in the middle of a 10 minute export (then a second export worked) all behaved correctly. One fix: a video with no sound track was reported as "the browser could not decode this file, convert it to MP3 or WAV", which is wrong and sent people to convert a fine file; it now says the video has no sound track and adds no sound. Note: on a narrow top bar the Audio button is inside the ... menu (also in the command palette: Export audio only). */window.AMIYO_EXPORT2_STEP=3;

