/* ==================== Script 1366 id="amiyo-export6-s10-verified" ==================== */
/* Export plan 2026-11, step 10 of 20 (Render queue), checked with real queue runs (MP4, headless Chrome), files read back with ffprobe.
   Found: the top bar "Queue" button opened an old queue that records in real time, can only make WebM and ignores the Export dialog (range, name template, fast export, burned-in timecode, file info, Include switches); the newer "Export queue" (Pr tools) ran the real dialog but gave every file the name "Untitled Video", treated a job as done without checking a file was saved, ended a job after the FIRST part of a split export (so the next job started while part 2 was still being made), quietly ignored a size or split the dialog does not have, had no way to reorder, and lost the list on reload.
   Fixed / improved: the top bar Queue button now opens the Export queue. Each job exports the whole edit through the normal dialog and is named as typed (your saved name template is left as it was). A job is "done" only when a file was saved ("N files saved"); otherwise it fails with a plain reason, and the queue carries on. A split job waits for all its parts (3 parts of a 14 s edit: 5 / 5 / 4 s). Reorder with the arrows, Copy, Remove, Retry, Cancel this job (queue continues), Stop queue (rest stay waiting), Clear finished. My presets can be added as jobs (size, frame rate, sound, format, bitrate and name template kept; checked: 24 fps, no sound, named file). The list is kept in this browser: a reload mid-job shows "interrupted", the canvas shape the job had set is flagged with a one-tap "Put it back", and "Resume queue" carries on with the interrupted job and the ones after it. The Pr tools "Export presets" (Export now / Add to queue) still feed the same queue.
   Not tested here: a failed job caused by running out of storage (step 19) and a queue of long (10 min+) jobs. */window.AMIYO_EXPORT6_STEP=10;
window.AMIYO_EXPORT7_STEP=6;

