/* Export plan 2026-11, step 12 of 20 (Speed, reverse and freeze-frame), checked with real exports of a test clip whose colour shows the source time, read back with ffmpeg. Freeze frame (2 s hold at 1 s): the picture is held for the whole hold and the clip carries on from the same frame afterwards. Reverse (picture and sound): the picture plays backwards from the end of the clip and the reversed sound is heard. 0.5x: the picture follows the right moment of the clip all the way. 2x: sound present and the length is right.
   Fault fixed: at 2x the exported picture fell further and further behind and repeated frames (at the end it showed the clip's 2.0 s instead of 2.9 s). Sped-up clips are exported with the live recorder (fast export does not take speed changes), and that recorder seeked the video one frame at a time, which cannot keep up. A sped-up clip now runs natively during the live recording and is re-aimed sooner (0.1 s instead of 0.3 s); the picture now stays within about 0.1 s of the right moment instead of up to 0.9 s behind. Normal-speed exports are not touched (checked again).
   Not tested here: speed ramps (keyframed speed) and the pitch of sped-up sound (step 16). * / */window.AMIYO_EXPORT6_STEP=12;

