/* ==================== Script 1369 id="amiyo-export6-s15-verified" ==================== */
/* Export plan 2026-11, step 15 of 20 (Colour and effects parity, preview versus export), checked with real exports (MP4 fast export, WebM, 480p size, live-recorder fallback) of a test picture / clip with colour patches, read back with ffmpeg and compared with the preview canvas at 6 sample points per case.
   Checked, all within about 3-5 levels of the preview (grain is random): every filter in the Filters list, a half-strength filter, 15 colour effects (brightness, contrast, saturation, grayscale, sepia, hue, invert, blur and the Lumetri-style sliders), sharpen, mirror, posterize, pixelate, grain, vignette, the 6 Looks, colour wheels, a filter + effects + look together, clip opacity, 13 adjustment-layer effects and an adjustment layer over a filtered clip (123 cases). The same cases on a video clip through the live recorder matched too once each clip was longer than 1.5 s (on a very slow machine a 0.6 s clip can show the neighbouring clip's colour because the recorder runs behind real time; not a colour fault).
   Faults fixed: (1) Looks and LUTs were graded on a copy only 480 px wide and stretched back up, so any clip with a Look or LUT came out soft in the exported file (a 1-pixel line test pattern became flat grey, edge contrast 255 -> 0). The export now grades at the full picture width (fast export) or up to 1280 (live recorder, so it keeps up); playing keeps 480 and a paused picture uses the preview width, so the preview is sharper too (edge contrast kept at 255 in the file). (2) LUTs picked the NEAREST table point, which gave visible banding (a 17-point LUT turned a smooth 256-step ramp into 79 steps in the file). LUTs now blend between table points (trilinear): 251 steps. Cost: a clip with a Look or LUT exports a little slower (about 2x on a slow test machine, 4 s of 720p graded video in about 8.5 s instead of 4.4 s).
   Not changed: the file is tagged full-range (pc) by the browser's encoder; players that ignore the tag show slightly stronger contrast. Not tested here: keyframed filter strength and LUT files loaded from disk (the table is read as before). */window.AMIYO_EXPORT6_STEP=15;

