/* ==================== Script 1373 id="amiyo-export6-s19-verified" ==================== */
/* Export plan 2026-11, step 19 of 20 (Error handling), checked in headless Chrome (phone size) with simulated faults.
   Already good: a clip whose file is gone gives a "BEFORE YOU EXPORT - Media missing: <name> will export blank. Import the file again to relink it" box with Export anyway / Go back (checked: both buttons 44 px, Export anyway carries on).
   Found: (1) nothing warned about low storage before an export; (2) a failed write to the chosen folder always said the same thing, whatever the cause (drive full, folder moved or deleted, no permission); (3) "Export stopped" and "The fast export could not finish" showed the browser's raw text (e.g. "The quota has been exceeded", "Array buffer allocation failed", "The requested file could not be read, typically due to permission problems..."); (4) after leaving the app during an export the only sign was a short message that disappears, and it could be missed.
   Fixed: (1) the Export dialog shows an amber "Low storage" note when the size estimate (times the number of files) is more than about 80% of what the browser reports free; (2) folder save failures say "the drive for <folder> is full", "the folder was moved or deleted - tap Change folder", or "no permission - tap Change folder and allow access", and the file is still downloaded; (3) raw errors are turned into plain words with one plain next step (storage: free some space; memory: close other tabs, Draft or 720p, 10-minute parts; unreadable file: import it again); (4) after you come back the progress card shows how many seconds you were away and what it may mean for fast or standard export, and the same note stays in the "Your video is ready" box.
   Checked: simulated 2 MB free (note shown) and plenty free (no note); simulated full drive and no permission on the chosen folder (right message, file downloaded); simulated "quota exceeded" in the middle of a standard export (plain message, progress screen closed, project safe); 3 s away during fast and standard export (note on progress card and in the result box, right wording for each). No page errors.
   Not tested here: a really full disk, a real background tab on a phone (the test machine cannot hide a tab, so hiding was simulated), a file deleted from a phone while exporting. */window.AMIYO_EXPORT6_STEP=19;

